{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment of C4, request 7555a333. Hugh decided the change on 14\nNovember: a draft keeps its basis.\n\nC4 takes D12 rule 5 as section 6 of\n`notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md` states it, from its first\nbuild. No build holds the old rule.\n\n1. A draft is a partial act with the `ref` of the row that it\n   opened on. `submit` builds the intent on that basis. It does not\n   build it at the replica's head.\n2. A draft submits the fields that the member changed, for an act\n   whose fields are optional.\n3. At the submit, the instance explores the act with the E1\n   function. If an `observed` basis has moved, the draft returns\n   before any signature, with the reason, the changed fields and\n   `now`.\n4. A submit of a returned draft is a new version on the basis\n   `now`. It keeps the request's key.\n5. The generated suite checks rule 1 with one case: a draft opened\n   at one head and submitted two heads later does not overwrite\n   another member's field.\n\nC4 now needs E1 on main as well as C3. Request E3 holds the rest of\nsection 6 and the view's `explore`, `offers`, `ref` and `recorded`.\nBuild C4 and E3 as one head if that is cheaper, and tell me first.\nThe other parts of 7555a333 stand.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}